    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d782">

                <pb facs="1259" n="1163" sameAs="frus:frus1874/pg1163"/>

                <head>No. 779.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Fish to Aristarchi Bey.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1874-05-26"><hi rendition="#italic">May</hi> 26,
                        1874</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to your note of the 19th of March
                    last, in regard to the measurement of vessels and tonnage dues on the Suez
                    Canal, and to my reply of the 24th of the same month, I have the honor to
                    inclose herewith a copy of a letter, under date of the 20th instant, addressed
                    to this Department by the Secretary of the Treasury, containing his views upon
                    the subject.</p>
                <p>I avail myself, &amp;c,</p>
                <closer><signed>HAMILTON FISH.</signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d782-a1.xml" xpointer="d782-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
